From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] manager: service timers while event queue is busy

The manager advanced its 250 ms timer only when pthread_cond_timedwait expired.
Under sustained metrics, topology, or bus traffic the event queue could remain
non-empty, so no timed wait occurred and all orchestration and periodic timers
were starved indefinitely.

Track the next deadline with a monotonic clock and service due ticks after each
event as well as after an idle wait. Bound catch-up to one second of ticks so a
long handler cannot cause an unbounded burst, then resume cadence from the
current time.

This restores the intended timer contract without adding a second thread or
allowing timer handlers to race event handlers.

Upstream-Status: Pending
